# Files the Vercel CLI must never upload.
#
# .env.local is the dangerous one: it holds APP_URL=http://localhost:4177, and
# the run doc records that APP_URL is what password-reset and confirmation links
# are built from. If it were uploaded, a deployment could resolve its own links
# back to localhost. Production configuration comes from the Vercel project's
# environment variables instead — never from a file in this directory.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build output and dependencies are rebuilt in the cloud; uploading them only
# risks shipping a stale build or a localhost-compiled artifact.
.next
node_modules

# Local logs and probe output.
*.log
*.log.err

# Local development tooling: probe scripts, the run doc, and test accounts.
# Nothing here is needed to build or run the application, and it has no business
# travelling inside a deployment's source.
.freebuff

# `apk/taskcash-pro` is a standalone UI prototype (mock data, no backend). It has
# its own package.json and is not part of this application's build, so it must
# not travel inside a deployment's source.
apk
